<tr><td style="padding:24px 30px;background:#CC1F2F;color:#ffffff;"><h1 style="margin:0;font-size:22px;color:#ffffff;">Panel Review Instructions</h1><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:13px;">CUGH 2027 Conference Panel Proposals</p></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:28px 30px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;">
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;">Dear EPC Member,</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;">Thank you for serving as a member to review the <strong>CUGH 2027 Conference Panel Proposals</strong>. Your evaluations help ensure the conference showcases timely, inclusive, and high-quality sessions that advance global health.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;">Please review each panel proposal using the criteria below, assigning a score from <strong>1 to 10</strong> for each category based on the quality, clarity, and alignment with CUGH’s goals and values. Use the scale provided as a guide, and consider how well the proposal contributes to interdisciplinary dialogue, addresses contemporary challenges, and elevates diverse voices in global health.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:17px;margin:22px 0 10px;">High-quality panel proposals should:</h2>
<ul style="margin:0 0 20px;padding-left:22px;">
<li>Fit within one of the six conference tracks</li>
<li>Offer innovative, solution-oriented content that can impact contemporary or future challenges</li>
<li>Feature a diversity of speakers by geography, discipline, gender, and institution</li>
<li>Be feasible within the 75-minute session format</li>
<li>Inspire learning and action that can inform policy, practice, or research</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:17px;margin:22px 0 10px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid #e4e9f0;">Scoring Scale (1–10)</h2>
<table width="100%" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="margin-bottom:22px;border:1px solid #e4e9f0;">
<tr style="background:#fff3f3;"><td width="60"><strong>1–3</strong></td><td>Poor – Criteria not met or very weakly addressed</td></tr>
<tr style="background:#fff9ea;"><td><strong>4–6</strong></td><td>Fair – Criteria partially met with limited detail or clarity</td></tr>
<tr style="background:#eef8fc;"><td><strong>7–8</strong></td><td>Good – Criteria met with appropriate detail and relevance</td></tr>
<tr style="background:#eef8f0;"><td><strong>9–10</strong></td><td>Excellent – Criteria strongly met with clear, compelling content and alignment to CUGH goals</td></tr>
</table>

<h2 style="font-size:17px;margin:22px 0 10px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid #e4e9f0;">Evaluation Criteria</h2>
<ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Relevance to Conference Track</strong><br>Does the panel clearly align with one of the six conference tracks?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Clarity of the Panel Description</strong><br>Is the panel description clear and are the panel’s goals well-defined, focused, and achievable within the session?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Topical Relevance &amp; Innovation</strong><br>Does the panel address a current or emerging global health issue or innovation?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Potential to Inform Knowledge, Policy or Outcomes</strong><br>Is the panel solution-oriented, focused on actionable ideas that could result in impact and outcomes that could inform policy or practice?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Diversity and Inclusion of Panelists</strong><br>Does the panel include a diversity of speakers (e.g., geography, gender, institution, discipline)? Does it include at least one speaker from a low- or middle-income country (LMIC)?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Expertise and Complementarity of Speakers</strong><br>Are the speakers qualified and does the proposal clearly demonstrate how their expertise complements one another?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Feasibility within the Panel Format</strong><br>Is the proposed content well-suited for the 75-minute format (presentations, discussion, audience Q&amp;A)?</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>Overall Quality and Impact</strong><br>Is the proposal well-written, organized, and compelling? Does it stand out as innovative or likely to engage the audience?</li>
</ol>

